                        "entry_id": "3dd01c4e-31ba-38c7-95d1-802c1c567c24",
                        "glosses": [
                            "That which clinches; that which makes something final or firm; a decisive factor."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c637f3a-8fb3-4004-9cc4-d58e0571ba57",
                                "sense_id": "6c1bcca0-6de5-3906-8431-516b11ff0fb2",
                                "text": "The clincher was that we couldn't wait any longer to leave, or it would get dark."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0d36d7bb-b770-4f5c-83c8-eb8613cef7bb",
                                "sense_id": "6c1bcca0-6de5-3906-8431-516b11ff0fb2",
                                "text": "Newcastle's Dan Gosling was sent off for a foul on Russell Martin but Ba fired in to cut the deficit, before Holt nodded in the clincher."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8dc448e1-5b57-4b74-8cc3-fca64efa4765",
                                "sense_id": "6c1bcca0-6de5-3906-8431-516b11ff0fb2",
                                "text": "Even after what turned out to be the clincher, Hakim Ziyech, Kai Havertz and Jorginho went close to forcing a penalty shootout."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac95d258-b47f-49cd-b9c3-fe3816040c03",
                                "sense_id": "6c1bcca0-6de5-3906-8431-516b11ff0fb2",
                                "text": "Transport Scotland acknowledges that the permanence of the new fares regime could be the clincher in persuading people to \"travel more often and make long-term choices with certainty, helping people to leave the car at home\"."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
